* sky130-gcedram -- loaded four-row 2T gain-cell column (issue #45, Epic #24
* phase 2). One bitline pair (bl_0 write / rbl_0 read), four rows. This is a
* characterization deck, NOT a sense amplifier: no sense decision is made and
* nothing here is an offset/yield validation. See sim/loaded-column/README.md.
*
* CONNECTIVITY comes from layout/array_topology.py build_topology(4, 1)
* (wl_r/rwl_r per row, bl_0/rbl_0 per column, sn_r_0 per cell); the DEVICE
* CARDS come from design/gain_cell_2t.spice (model, W, L and instance
* parameters parsed out of its two device lines by run_loaded_column.py), so
* no device is restated by hand. The cell block below is generated by the
* runner and substituted at the CELLS token below.
*
* ALL TIMING / BIAS / LOADING in the .param block is a labelled ASSUMPTION
* (proposed engineering choice pending the spec decision process), except
* VDD, TEDGE and the write-pulse width, which reuse the committed
* sim/bitcell-transient/ conventions (1.8 V, 100 ps, 20 ns write pulse, plain
* 1.8 V wordlines, active-low read select on rwl, rbl bias VDD/2).
* The runner parses this block for its measurement instants.

.param VDD     = 1.8
.param VRBL    = 0.9
.param TEDGE   = 100p
.param TW0     = 1n
.param TWSTEP  = 25n
.param TWPULSE = 20n
.param TBL_LAG = 2n
.param THOLD0  = 100n
.param TPRE_GAP = 2n
.param TREAD_PULSE = 20n
.param TTAIL   = 5n
.param T_READ  = 110n
* per-case parameters, re-set between cases by alterparam in the .control block
.param B0 = 0
.param B1 = 0
.param B2 = 0
.param B3 = 0
.param SL0 = 0
.param SL1 = 0
.param SL2 = 0
.param SL3 = 0
.param C_RBL   = @@C_RBL@@

.lib "@@PDK_NGSPICE_LIB@@" @@CORNER@@
.temp @@TEMP_C@@

@@CELLS@@

* Declared bitline loading (ASSUMPTION, schematic level -- NOT extracted): a
* lumped capacitor on rbl_0 standing in for column wire + sense-input load.
* The four M_RD drain junctions are already in the device models; the write
* bitline bl_0 is an ideal driver (its loading is irrelevant to the result).
c_rbl rbl_0 0 {C_RBL}

* Write: row r's wordline pulses 0 -> VDD -> 0 at TW0 + r*TWSTEP; bl_0 is held
* at that row's data level for the pulse and returns to 0 TBL_LAG after the
* wordline is fully low (the cell is never written by a bitline transition).
@@WRITE_SOURCES@@

* Idle / hold bias: rwl_r = VDD (deselected), bl_0 = 0, rbl_0 held at VRBL
* through a precharge switch. In the read the selected row's rwl falls.
@@RWL_SOURCES@@

* Precharge: ideal switch (Ron 100 ohm, Roff 1e12) from a VRBL source to
* rbl_0, closed until TPRE_GAP before the read, then rbl_0 floats on C_RBL.
vpre   pre 0 dc {VRBL}
vctl   ctl 0 pwl(0 {VDD} {T_READ-TPRE_GAP} {VDD} {T_READ-TPRE_GAP+TEDGE} 0)
.model swpre sw(vt=0.9 vh=0.1 ron=100 roff=1e12)
spre   pre rbl_0 ctl 0 swpre

.ic v(rbl_0)={VRBL}
@@ICS@@

.control
set filetype=ascii
@@CASES@@
.endc

.end
